WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.531
First, create your portfolio.

2
00:00:02.531 --> 00:00:05.803
This walkthrough uses a demo account.

3
00:00:05.803 --> 00:00:09.620
Click the plus beside the portfolio selector.

4
00:00:09.620 --> 00:00:17.799
Enter a portfolio name, keep P S X Stocks selected, and choose an available broker.

5
00:00:17.799 --> 00:00:19.435
Click Create Portfolio.

6
00:00:19.435 --> 00:00:22.161
Next, configure your broker charges.

7
00:00:23.430 --> 00:00:25.516
Open Settings, then Broker Setup.

8
00:00:25.516 --> 00:00:29.271
Add New Broker lets you enter a new broker.

9
00:00:29.271 --> 00:00:35.112
Here, click the pencil to configure the Demo Broker already selected for our portfolio.

10
00:00:35.112 --> 00:00:41.370
Check the name and enter the email sender address if you want to import confirmations.

11
00:00:41.370 --> 00:00:44.708
Choose the commission rule from your broker tariff.

12
00:00:44.708 --> 00:00:50.131
This example uses the higher of a percentage or a rate per share.

13
00:00:50.131 --> 00:00:55.555
Check both rates, the sales tax percentage, and the C D C charge.

14
00:00:55.555 --> 00:00:59.310
These are example figures; use your own broker charges.

15
00:00:59.310 --> 00:01:03.482
Add annual maintenance only if applicable, then click Update Config.

16
00:01:05.550 --> 00:01:08.609
Click the pencil beside your portfolio name.

17
00:01:08.609 --> 00:01:12.104
Confirm the default broker and save your changes.

18
00:01:12.104 --> 00:01:15.163
New transactions use that broker fee configuration.

19
00:01:15.163 --> 00:01:19.532
You are now ready to add your cash and trades.

20
00:01:20.790 --> 00:01:22.312
Open Add Transaction.

21
00:01:22.312 --> 00:01:26.876
In the Manual tab, choose Cash, Deposit or Withdrawal.

22
00:01:26.876 --> 00:01:31.948
Keep Add Funds selected, enter your deposit amount, and save.

23
00:01:31.948 --> 00:01:36.512
This records your cash; it does not transfer money.

24
00:01:37.790 --> 00:01:41.113
Open Add Transaction again, and switch to Buy.

25
00:01:41.113 --> 00:01:44.020
Enter the stock symbol, quantity, and price.

26
00:01:44.020 --> 00:01:49.834
Here we enter one hundred O G D C shares at two hundred rupees.

27
00:01:49.834 --> 00:01:53.572
Always use your actual trade date and broker records.

28
00:01:54.830 --> 00:01:59.913
Scroll down and check the fees and taxes against your contract note.

29
00:01:59.913 --> 00:02:02.031
The total includes those charges.

30
00:02:02.031 --> 00:02:06.267
Click Save Transaction to add the purchase to your portfolio.

31
00:02:07.550 --> 00:02:10.287
Your purchase now appears in Holdings.

32
00:02:10.287 --> 00:02:13.024
Average price includes the purchase costs.

33
00:02:13.024 --> 00:02:15.761
Current value uses the current price.

34
00:02:15.761 --> 00:02:20.779
Daily profit and loss measures the change from the previous close.

35
00:02:20.779 --> 00:02:26.710
Total profit and loss compares value with the cost of your open position.

36
00:02:26.710 --> 00:02:28.991
These prices are demonstration figures.

37
00:02:30.270 --> 00:02:31.796
Open Reports, then Transactions.

38
00:02:31.796 --> 00:02:35.611
Both the cash deposit and stock purchase are listed here.

39
00:02:35.611 --> 00:02:42.097
This is where you can review your entries and use Edit when you need to correct one.

40
00:02:43.350 --> 00:02:46.911
Check for the green Synced status in the sidebar.

41
00:02:46.911 --> 00:02:51.659
On the live app, your portfolio backup stays in your Google Drive.

42
00:02:51.659 --> 00:02:54.825
Use the same account on your next device.

43
00:02:54.825 --> 00:02:58.782
Next, let us look at faster ways to enter trades.

44
00:03:00.070 --> 00:03:05.615
For A I scanning, you need to add your own Gemini A P I key.

45
00:03:05.615 --> 00:03:08.203
Open Settings, then A P I Keys.

46
00:03:08.203 --> 00:03:14.857
Get Key opens Google A I Studio, where you can create a key for a free tier project.

47
00:03:14.857 --> 00:03:16.336
Free usage has limits.

48
00:03:16.336 --> 00:03:20.772
Paste your key into Gemini A I Key and click Save Configuration.

49
00:03:20.772 --> 00:03:24.469
The other keys are not required for A I scan.

50
00:03:24.469 --> 00:03:28.166
Keep your key private; this example uses a dummy key.

51
00:03:30.070 --> 00:03:33.309
Open Add Transaction and choose A I Scan.

52
00:03:33.309 --> 00:03:34.928
Upload a broker confirmation.

53
00:03:34.928 --> 00:03:40.595
You can use a screenshot, P D F, Excel, or C S V file.

54
00:03:40.595 --> 00:03:44.239
Here we use a sample C S V confirmation.

55
00:03:44.239 --> 00:03:46.263
Click Analyze with A I.

56
00:03:46.263 --> 00:03:49.906
Gemini reads the document and prepares trades for review.

57
00:03:51.190 --> 00:03:57.290
Check the trade date, symbol, quantity, price, and each fee against your broker's confirmation.

58
00:03:57.290 --> 00:03:59.905
Correct any mistakes in the table.

59
00:03:59.905 --> 00:04:01.648
Scanning can make errors.

60
00:04:01.648 --> 00:04:06.441
Select the rows you want to keep, then click Add Selected.

61
00:04:06.441 --> 00:04:09.927
Close the window to see the updated holdings.

62
00:04:11.190 --> 00:04:15.440
You can also scan a confirmation directly from Gmail.

63
00:04:15.440 --> 00:04:17.800
Open Add Transaction, then Email.

64
00:04:17.800 --> 00:04:23.466
Enter your broker's sender address and a subject keyword, such as Confirmation.

65
00:04:23.466 --> 00:04:25.827
Click Find Emails with Attachments.

66
00:04:25.827 --> 00:04:32.438
If Google asks for Gmail permission, review and approve it using the same account.

67
00:04:32.438 --> 00:04:35.271
This demonstration uses a sample email.

68
00:04:36.550 --> 00:04:38.144
Click the broker attachment.

69
00:04:38.144 --> 00:04:43.325
It opens in A I Scan, using the Gemini key you saved earlier.

70
00:04:43.325 --> 00:04:50.499
Click Analyze with A I, review the extracted rows, and add only trades you have not already recorded.

71
00:04:50.499 --> 00:04:56.477
This is the same confirmation we imported earlier, so we will not add it again.

72
00:04:56.477 --> 00:05:02.455
You can now record trades manually, scan a document, or import a broker email attachment.

73
00:05:03.710 --> 00:05:12.360
When Drive sync completes, your portfolio data, settings, and saved A P I keys are backed up to your own Google Drive.

74
00:05:12.360 --> 00:05:16.292
P S X Tracker does not make these backups public.

75
00:05:16.292 --> 00:05:21.404
Access follows your Google account permissions, including access you grant to the app.

76
00:05:21.404 --> 00:05:24.943
A local copy is also kept on your device.

77
00:05:24.943 --> 00:05:29.661
Login, alert, and connection records are stored separately to run those features.

78
00:05:29.661 --> 00:05:35.559
When you use A I scanning, the selected document is sent to Google for processing.
